Strict Formatting Rules for 3mm to 4mm Cells
The Double-Digit Trap: A 3mm or 3.5mm cell is incredibly narrow. If your color palette has more than 9 colors, you will have double digits (e.g., 10, 18). A Regular font might be too wide horizontally, forcing you to use a Light or Condensed font weight so the two digits fit inside the cell boundaries.
Font Choice Matters: Stick to ultra-clean, uniform lines like Arial Regular/Light or Inter Light. Avoid fonts like Times New Roman where some parts of the number are thick and other parts are whisper-thin.
Color Adjustments: If you drop down to a 3mm cell with a 3pt Light font, change your font color to 60% Black (Dark Gray). If you use a 30% light gray on a font that microscopic, the KDP printer won't lay down enough ink dots, and the number will look like it vanished.

